    <dashboard enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='Write Answers Here'>
      <style>
        <style-rule element='dash-text'>
          <format attr='vertical-align' id='dash-text_7' value='top' />
        </style-rule>
      </style>
      <size maxheight='800' maxwidth='1000' minheight='800' minwidth='1000' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='15' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98000' id='18' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98400' x='800' y='1000'>
            <zone h='5250' id='19' type-v2='title' w='98400' x='800' y='1000'>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='4' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
            <zone h='92750' id='16' type-v2='layout-basic' w='98400' x='800' y='6250' />
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='62125' id='3' type-v2='text' w='49200' x='1000' y='1250'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='10'>1. In the Net Production sheet, which regions are net energy producers? </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The regions that are net energy producers are</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>Mid-Atlantic, Northwest, Southwest, Central, Southeast</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='10'>2.  In the Supply and Demand By Region sheet, during which month is there the greatest energy surplus in the Mid Atlantic region? </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The greatest energy surplus in the Mid Atlantic region is in the month of August</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='10'>3. What are the top 3 regions in the percentage of renewable energy generated? </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The top 3 regions in the percentage of renewable energy generated are Northwest, Central, and California</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='10'>4. What two regions have some form of renewable energy as the top source? Cycle through the different regions to find your answer. </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The two regions that have some form of renewable energy as the top source are Central and Northwest</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='10'>5. </run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>During what time of the day is California generating the most wind energy, in other words, what hours of the day is Percent Difference &gt; 0? </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>California is generating the most wind energy at 3pm</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>8. What Region would you recommend Intel put their next data center?</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>After careful analysis of the energy production and availability data, the Northwest region emerges as the most strategic location for Intel’s next data center. The Northwest ranks 2nd in Net Production of energy, which suggests a reliable and potentially cost-effective supply of electricity. Moreover, it ranks highest in the percentage of renewable energy generation among all regions, with renewable sources serving as the primary contributor to its energy mix with 41.92% overall. Hydropower and Pumped Storage is the Northwest’s leading energy source. These factors align closely with Intel’s long-term goals of operational efficiency, energy security, and environmental sustainability, positioning the Northwest as an ideal candidate for future investment.</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Æ </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>Æ </run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Æ </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The Central region also presents a strong case, offering a surplus of energy production and a significant reliance on renewable sources. Like the Northwest, the Central region has renewable energy as its leading source, which supports Intel’s commitment to reducing its carbon footprint. However, the Northwest offers a slightly stronger profile in terms of renewable energy leadership and established infrastructure for clean energy. Given these considerations, the Northwest region offers the best combination of economic and environmental advantages for Intel’s new data center development.</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Æ </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>9. (LevelUp) How would you describe the difference in Renewable Energy generated in the CAL and NW regions? </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The renewable energy generated in California starts low and to increases significantly  at 6am before it begins to drop significantly at 3pm. The Northwest does not have a large spike but its lowest generation of energy is more than California&apos;s peak point of energy generated. Although Northwest&apos;s energy generation does not have a large spike it&apos;s energy generation remains at a high level. </run>
          </formatted-text>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='4' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='79250' id='4' type-v2='text' w='98400' x='-100' y='60000'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontsize='14'>Double-Click to Edit</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Answer to Question 1: </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The regions that are net energy producers are</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>Mid-Atlantic, Northwest, Southwest, Central, Southeast</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Answer to Question 2:  </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The greatest energy surplus in the Mid Atlantic region is in the month of August</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000'>Answer to Question 3:  </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The top 3 regions in the percentage of renewable energy generated are Northwest, Central, and California</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000'>Answer to Question 4:  </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The two regions that have some form of renewable energy as the top source are Central and Northwest</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000'>Answer to Question 5: </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>California is generating the most wind energy at 3pm</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000'>Answer to Question 8: </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>After careful analysis of the energy production and availability data, the Northwest region emerges as the most strategic location for Intel’s next data center. The Northwest ranks 2nd in Net Production of energy, which suggests a reliable and potentially cost-effective supply of electricity. Moreover, it ranks highest in the percentage of renewable energy generation among all regions, with renewable sources serving as the primary contributor to its energy mix with 41.92% overall. Hydropower and Pumped Storage is the Northwest’s leading energy source. These factors align closely with Intel’s long-term goals of operational efficiency, energy security, and environmental sustainability, positioning the Northwest as an ideal candidate for future investment.</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Æ </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>Æ </run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Æ </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The Central region also presents a strong case, offering a surplus of energy production and a significant reliance on renewable sources. Like the Northwest, the Central region has renewable energy as its leading source, which supports Intel’s commitment to reducing its carbon footprint. However, the Northwest offers a slightly stronger profile in terms of renewable energy leadership and established infrastructure for clean energy. Given these considerations, the Northwest region offers the best combination of economic and environmental advantages for Intel’s new data center development.</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Æ </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000'>Answer to LevelUp: </run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The renewable energy generated in California starts low and to increases significantly  at 6am before it begins to drop significantly at 3pm. The Northwest does not have a large spike but its lowest generation of energy is more than California&apos;s peak point of energy generated. Although Northwest&apos;s energy generation does not have a large spike it&apos;s energy generation remains at a high level.</run>
          </formatted-text>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='4' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <devicelayouts>
        <devicelayout auto-generated='true' name='Phone'>
          <size maxheight='700' minheight='700' sizing-mode='vscroll' />
          <zones>
            <zone h='100000' id='67' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
              <zone h='98000' id='66' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98400' x='800' y='1000'>
                <zone h='5250' id='19' type-v2='title' w='98400' x='800' y='1000'>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='62125' id='3' type-v2='text' w='49200' x='1000' y='1250'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='10'>1. In the Net Production sheet, which regions are net energy producers? </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The regions that are net energy producers are</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>Mid-Atlantic, Northwest, Southwest, Central, Southeast</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='10'>2.  In the Supply and Demand By Region sheet, during which month is there the greatest energy surplus in the Mid Atlantic region? </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The greatest energy surplus in the Mid Atlantic region is in the month of August</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='10'>3. What are the top 3 regions in the percentage of renewable energy generated? </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The top 3 regions in the percentage of renewable energy generated are Northwest, Central, and California</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='10'>4. What two regions have some form of renewable energy as the top source? Cycle through the different regions to find your answer. </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The two regions that have some form of renewable energy as the top source are Central and Northwest</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='10'>5. </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>During what time of the day is California generating the most wind energy, in other words, what hours of the day is Percent Difference &gt; 0? </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>California is generating the most wind energy at 3pm</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>8. What Region would you recommend Intel put their next data center?</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>After careful analysis of the energy production and availability data, the Northwest region emerges as the most strategic location for Intel’s next data center. The Northwest ranks 2nd in Net Production of energy, which suggests a reliable and potentially cost-effective supply of electricity. Moreover, it ranks highest in the percentage of renewable energy generation among all regions, with renewable sources serving as the primary contributor to its energy mix with 41.92% overall. Hydropower and Pumped Storage is the Northwest’s leading energy source. These factors align closely with Intel’s long-term goals of operational efficiency, energy security, and environmental sustainability, positioning the Northwest as an ideal candidate for future investment.</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Æ </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>Æ </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Æ </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The Central region also presents a strong case, offering a surplus of energy production and a significant reliance on renewable sources. Like the Northwest, the Central region has renewable energy as its leading source, which supports Intel’s commitment to reducing its carbon footprint. However, the Northwest offers a slightly stronger profile in terms of renewable energy leadership and established infrastructure for clean energy. Given these considerations, the Northwest region offers the best combination of economic and environmental advantages for Intel’s new data center development.</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Æ </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>9. (LevelUp) How would you describe the difference in Renewable Energy generated in the CAL and NW regions? </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The renewable energy generated in California starts low and to increases significantly  at 6am before it begins to drop significantly at 3pm. The Northwest does not have a large spike but its lowest generation of energy is more than California&apos;s peak point of energy generated. Although Northwest&apos;s energy generation does not have a large spike it&apos;s energy generation remains at a high level. </run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='79250' id='4' type-v2='text' w='98400' x='-100' y='60000'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run fontsize='14'>Double-Click to Edit</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Answer to Question 1: </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The regions that are net energy producers are</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>Mid-Atlantic, Northwest, Southwest, Central, Southeast</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Answer to Question 2:  </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The greatest energy surplus in the Mid Atlantic region is in the month of August</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000'>Answer to Question 3:  </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The top 3 regions in the percentage of renewable energy generated are Northwest, Central, and California</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000'>Answer to Question 4:  </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The two regions that have some form of renewable energy as the top source are Central and Northwest</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000'>Answer to Question 5: </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>California is generating the most wind energy at 3pm</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000'>Answer to Question 8: </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>After careful analysis of the energy production and availability data, the Northwest region emerges as the most strategic location for Intel’s next data center. The Northwest ranks 2nd in Net Production of energy, which suggests a reliable and potentially cost-effective supply of electricity. Moreover, it ranks highest in the percentage of renewable energy generation among all regions, with renewable sources serving as the primary contributor to its energy mix with 41.92% overall. Hydropower and Pumped Storage is the Northwest’s leading energy source. These factors align closely with Intel’s long-term goals of operational efficiency, energy security, and environmental sustainability, positioning the Northwest as an ideal candidate for future investment.</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Æ </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>Æ </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Æ </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The Central region also presents a strong case, offering a surplus of energy production and a significant reliance on renewable sources. Like the Northwest, the Central region has renewable energy as its leading source, which supports Intel’s commitment to reducing its carbon footprint. However, the Northwest offers a slightly stronger profile in terms of renewable energy leadership and established infrastructure for clean energy. Given these considerations, the Northwest region offers the best combination of economic and environmental advantages for Intel’s new data center development.</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Æ </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000'>Answer to LevelUp: </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The renewable energy generated in California starts low and to increases significantly  at 6am before it begins to drop significantly at 3pm. The Northwest does not have a large spike but its lowest generation of energy is more than California&apos;s peak point of energy generated. Although Northwest&apos;s energy generation does not have a large spike it&apos;s energy generation remains at a high level.</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
              </zone>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='8' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
          </zones>
        </devicelayout>
      </devicelayouts>
      <simple-id uuid='{F4E163A0-9313-474F-84C2-16A4742115B4}' />
    </dashboard>
